Frequently questions like, such as "What is a good ((lujvo))/((fu'ivla)) for X?" comes up. This is an attempt to topically organize new answers to that question, and to store a bit of the discussion that goes along with those answers.

* ((Math terminology))
* ((Computer terminology))
* ((gerna tecyvla))
* ((Science terminology)) (Biology, Linguistics, Physics, etc)
* ((Medical terminology))
* ((Music terminology))
* ((Chess terminology))
* ((Radio terminology))
* ((Political terminology))
* ((Sports))
* ((Sexual terminology))
* ((Literary terminology))
** ((Lojban literary forms))
* ((Keyboard key names))
* ((Logicians' jargon|Logical terminology))
* ((valsi lo djedi e lo masti vu'o poi ropno))
* ((Vehicles terminology))
* ((Internet 'slang'))

Note that there is a terminology section on [http://www.lojban.org/jbovlaste/wiki/FrontPage|Jbovlaste's own Wiki], however, you have to have a ((Jbovlaste)) user to be able to make changes there.

You know, ((The Wiki)) is a wonderful thing, even easier than the web for this: when you use one of these creative ((lujvo)) etc., link it to its page or that of its category, to make looking it up easier, thus hopefully making it easier to get these accepted.  Lujvo aren't necessarily supposed to be completely transparent once you decode the ((rafsi)) (or else they'd be ((tanru))), so I'd say this is a good practice. ''--mi'e ((Mark Shoulson|mark.))''